data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:13:22.552219+00:00", "content": "Based on the telemetry and logs available for **ce_branch3**, here's what happened:\n\n## Key Event\nA **VRF route change** occurred on interface **eth1** at timestamp `1786018075` (Unix epoch) [events:0]. The FRR routing daemon logged this as a medium-severity event (`FRR-VRF-ROUTE-CHANGE`) with scenario ID `congestion-ce_branch3-b4432713`.\n\n## Current Health Status (Latest Metrics)\n- **Hardware**: All normal \u2014 fan 3000 RPM, power ~69 W, PSU 11.9 V, temperature 29.4 \u00b0C [metrics:0][metrics:1][metrics:2][metrics:3]\n- **Interface eth0 (WAN uplink)**: 110 queue drops and 1,825 input discards [metrics:6][metrics:26] \u2014 indicates past congestion/contention\n- **Interface eth1 (where VRF change occurred)**: Clean \u2014 0 queue drops, 0 discards, 0 errors [metrics:5][metrics:27][metrics:36]\n- **SD-WAN tunnel (wg0)**: Active, latency ~65 ms, jitter ~2.4 ms, loss ~0.2 % [topo:ce_branch3]\n- **Upstream PE (pe3)**: Healthy \u2014 BGP established (2 peers), OSPF neighbors up, MPLS LDP sessions up [topo:pe3]\n\n## Topology Context\nce_branch3 connects to **pe3** (provider edge), which uplinks to core routers **p7/p8** and hub **ce_hub3** \u2014 all currently reporting healthy metrics [topo:ce_branch3][topo:pe3][topo:p7][topo:p8][topo:ce_hub3].\n\n## Summary\nThe only recorded anomaly last month was a single **VRF route-change event on eth1**. The interface itself shows no errors/discards now, but the WAN-facing **eth0** has historical queue drops and input discards suggesting transient congestion. No logs for \"error\", \"fail\", or other fault patterns were found beyond this one VRF event.\n\n**Citations**: [events:0] [metrics:0] [metrics:1] [metrics:2] [metrics:3] [metrics:5] [metrics:6] [metrics:26] [metrics:27] [metrics:36] [topo:ce_branch3] [topo:pe3] [topo:p7] [topo:p8] [topo:ce_hub3]"}

